# Two cantilevers of the same shape, BEAM1 and BEAM2, each with C3D8 and C3D8I
# elements in its element set. hecmw1 puts the elements of each set in two
# sections by their element names, and !SECTION, SECNUM=1 gives FORM361=FI to
# all the elements of BEAM1, while all those of BEAM2 take IC, the default of
# a linear static analysis, so the tip of BEAM1 moves less than that of BEAM2.
!VERSION
 3
!SOLUTION, TYPE=STATIC
!SECTION, SECNUM=1, FORM361=FI
!BOUNDARY
 FIX, 1, 3, 0.0
!CLOAD
 TIP, 2, -0.01
!SOLVER, METHOD=CG, PRECOND=1, ITERLOG=NO, TIMELOG=NO
 10000, 1
 1.0e-10, 1.0, 0.0
!WRITE, RESULT
!END
